  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Let $a=\u27e80,0,3\u27e9$ and $b=\u27e82,0,1\u27e9.$ Find $a\\times b.$",
  "worked_solution": "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((0)(1)-(0)(3))i-((0)(1)-(2)(3))j+((0)(0)-(2)(0))k \\\\  & =(0-0)i-(0-6)j+(0-0)k \\\\  & =6j.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
